00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:39.280
Looking back at six episodes from 2026 May 18th to 2026 May 24th, the stories that mattered,

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:47.500
what we learned and what to watch next. This week, the NASDAQ composite traded between 25,871 and

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:57.580
26,344. The index posted a year-to-date gain of 13.16%. Our simulated portfolio sits at plus

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:05.320
0.48% year-to-date, producing an alpha of negative 12.68% against the NASDAQ benchmark.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:17.240
The S&amp;P 500 fluctuated between 7,354 and 7,473, while the TSX composite range from 33,741

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:25.480
to 34,471. Rotation out of broad technology into energy and healthcare names dominated sentiment

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:31.140
as oil volatility and sticky yields kept traders cautious across both US and Canadian markets.

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:36.300
The clearest pattern across the week was the repeated need for volume confirmation

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:42.600
before committing capital to momentum setups. Nvidia delivered a record quarter that included a

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:49.980
2,400% dividend increase yet the stock reactions stayed muted without volume above the 20-day average.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:56.740
That outcome reinforced why we now require share volume confirmation on any high profile earnings

00:01:56.740 --> 00:02:03.340
beat before scaling positions in the simulated book. Oil price spikes created a second order

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:09.940
opportunity for companies that can pass costs through without volume loss, screening for stable gross

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:15.220
margins over the prior two quarters and low customer concentration gave a practical filter that

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:21.600
worked across retailers and manufacturers facing input cost pressure. The Luda lemon proxy

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:26.940
battle showed how founder board clashes become actionable when ownership concentration is high

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:34.200
and activist stakes exceed 5%. Retail investors who monitor proxy filings and shareholder letters

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:39.500
gained an early window into governance risk that can drive volatility around annual meetings.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:46.000
PayPal offered a buyback compounding example at roughly 6.5 times free cash flow

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:52.580
with $6 billion in annual free cash flow. Holding through the period of depressed sentiment while

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:58.080
the share count shrinks creates a setup that can compound even before a re-rating arrives.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:06.140
The SEC cleared NASDAQ Bitcoin index options on VLX, opening cash settled European style contracts

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:12.220
that Canadian investors can consider inside registered accounts once CFTC clearance follows.

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:19.080
These contracts provide defined risk and simpler tax treatment compared with futures or spot holdings.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:25.300
The most consequential development of the week was Nvidia's volume lesson, which echoed in our

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:32.620
own simulated snowflake trade that closed up 0.40%, yet still required the same filter.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:39.180
Looking ahead, factory activity data and any follow-through on the Bitcoin options decision

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:44.780
should give directional clues for next week. With US and Canadian markets closed today,

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:50.400
we use the time to review what the week's simulated positions taught us about entry discipline.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:56.480
The recurring theme is that clean technical setups without volume confirmation above the 20-day

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:01.080
average tend to produce muted follow-through even when fundamentals are solid.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:06.820
On the international side, Asian and European markets showed similar rotation toward resource

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:13.360
names as energy inflation pressures persisted. Crypto markets traded 24-7 and the new options

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:19.000
approval suggest regulated exposure will become easier to access inside tax advantage to counts.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:25.360
Longer horizon investors should prepare for Monday by watching whether AI leadership regains volume

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:32.040
supported momentum or continues to seed ground to value and energy themes. The practical takeaway is

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:37.900
simple. Add a volume confirmation step to every momentum screen before entering new positions.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:44.280
Before we wrap, watch for fresh options flow data on Monday that could confirm whether institutions

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:50.500
